scripts/ - repo-level helper scripts
====================================

    gen-compdb.sh   compatibility entry point for make compdb
    gen-compdb.py   serialize/merge JSON from the makefiles' CC/CFLAGS
    test_compdb.py  isolated path, profile, flag and compiler checks

Use it
------
    make compdb                    # -> ./compile_commands.json (git-ignored)
    make compdb PROFILE=asan CC=clang
    sh scripts/gen-compdb.sh       # same target; forwards make arguments
    make test-compdb               # regression, also run by CI

Requires Python 3. The makefiles export their actual CC/CFLAGS, including
optimization, optional readline and the profile's generated install-path header.
Test sources also receive -UNDEBUG. Static-library and CLI translation units
are included; link commands and RTL test-vector generators are not included.
Generating the database prepares the header but does not compile the software.

The database uses JSON argument arrays: spaces/quotes in paths and compiler
arguments are preserved. Publication replaces the file only after successful
generation. Regenerate after changing profile, compiler, flags or source lists.
Absolute paths make it machine-specific and git-ignored. `bear -- make` is an
alternative for capturing an actual build (bear is in the Nix dev shell).
